==Battleground==
*2 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Devil Wife]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Fallen Bear]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Devil Wife|Devil Wives]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**5 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A [[Shield Piercing|Shield Piercer]] like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] or [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] is near essential here, [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immune]] backliners can contribute a lot but aren't essential and anti-Aku meatshields can be very helpful. [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]], [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] and [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] are great candidates for this role. That being said, you don't need to bring anti-Aku meatshields, generalists are still viable, like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] or [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|erasers]]. The Death Surges are something to watch out for if you are using generalist meatshields so you might still want to reconsider using dual erasers. Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] paired with good meatshielding can deal with basically all of the enemies in this stage, but just make sure to watch your money.

